  "notes": [
    "New analyst requirements and architect design candidates originate from known gateway responses, with exact call, settled usage, contract, content and source-event bindings. Model origin does not verify content.",
    "Historical authenticated-Worker candidates keep their original origin and event shape; manual publication and schema validity do not confer model provenance.",
    "Both real role tasks remain submitted, producer_verified=false, verified=false and counts_as_success=false. Hard dependencies and Gate-V remain unchanged; the independent second model is pending configuration.",
    "Two separately recorded real Flash responses; role generation executes no code, file, network tool or Docker. Full-suite model HTTP uses mocks. Seventeen existing Docker regression tests remain in the full infrastructure stage.",
    "The design request consumes explicitly approved typed requirements under its current claim/epoch. Preview reads and grants alone do not dispatch models or verify content. No automatic retry or grant inheritance.",
    "Named local identities are route permissions, not production OIDC or proof of independent people. API/Store use SQLite; PostgreSQL integration tests validate separate DDL, roles and constraints.",
    "Actual private UTF-8 and UTF-16LE values are scanned in public files and decompressed archive contents, including historical archives. Scan output never contains the values.",
    "Raw CRLF exception paths preserve generated/upstream bytes; other source is LF. Manifest excludes itself; archive hash is delivered separately. Browser logs, credentials, databases, venvs, runtime images and native server binaries are excluded.",
    "Desktop 4.70.0 runtime socket workaround is unchanged; full workflow, production identity, recovery and scale validation remain incomplete. Nothing is published publicly."
